---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const description =
  'The SSSF 2.0 CLI: project initialization, flows, ticket machine, sandbox operations, and visualizer.';
---
<DocsLayout
  title="CLI reference"
  description={description}
  current="/docs/cli"
  prev={{ href: '/docs/visualizer', label: 'Visualizer' }}
  next={{ href: '/docs/core-concepts', label: 'Core concepts' }}
>
  <p>
    <span class="cmd">sssf</span> is a global CLI. Version 2.0 uses a hidden
    <code class="hl">.adws/</code> footprint and makes flows the only work-entry surface.
    Legacy projects must run <span class="cmd">sssf init</span> before using a flow.
  </p>

  <h2>Setup and projects</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf --version</code></td><td>Print the installed version (2.0.0).</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf init [--project P] [--refresh] [--force] [--auto]</code></td><td>
        Stamp the hidden <code class="hl">.adws/</code> footprint and register the project.
        On a legacy <code class="hl">adws/</code> project, back up the old tree to
        <code class="hl">sssf-&lt;timestamp&gt;/</code>, preserve and migrate only its database,
        then stamp a fresh footprint and warn about customizations that need to be reapplied.
      </td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf projects [list | remove &lt;name&gt;]</code></td><td>List or remove registered projects.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf doctor</code></td><td>Check global prerequisites.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf upgrade [--check]</code></td><td>Upgrade the CLI or check whether an update is available.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Flows</h2>
  <p>Flows are the only way to start project work. All flow commands require the new <code class="hl">.adws/</code> layout.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf flow plan [&lt;ticket-id&gt;] [--skip-exploration] [--revise]</code></td><td>Explore and plan an idea into a spec and ready-for-agent implementation tickets.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf flow implement &lt;ticket-id&gt;</code></td><td>Implement one ready-for-agent ticket through triage, build, and review.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf flow implement afk [--cap N] [--wait-seconds S]</code></td><td>Work the ready-for-agent queue one ticket per run.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf flow deploy [--yes] [--down] [--revert &lt;ticket-id&gt;]</code></td><td>Sign off the dev snapshot and run the release train; optionally tear down the workbench or revert a ticket before the MR.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Ticket machine</h2>
  <p>Ticketing is configured per project in <code class="hl">.adws/config/ticketing.yaml</code>.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf ticket new "&lt;title&gt;"</code></td><td>Create a title-only idea ticket in needs-triage.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf ticket sync [--provider jira|linear|github|gitlab]</code></td><td>Pull external tickets, then mirror machine labels, completion, and rejection comments. This is the only tracker writer.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf ticket list [--backlog]</code></td><td>List tickets or only ready-for-agent tickets.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf ticket context &lt;ticket-id&gt; [--set TEXT]</code></td><td>Read or save context for a ticket.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf ticket backlog &lt;ticket-id&gt; [--feedback TEXT]</code></td><td>Requeue an eligible ticket to ready-for-agent.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Operations</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf sandbox build</code></td><td>Build or refresh the runner image.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf sandbox list</code></td><td>Show active sandboxes.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf sandbox stop &lt;adw-id&gt;</code></td><td>Stop a live run; its worktree remains available for review.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf sandbox restart &lt;adw-id&gt;</code></td><td>Restart a run on its existing sandbox branch.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf sweep [--project P] [--days N]</code></td><td>Archive old sessions and clean up their sandbox resources.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf heal [start|stop|status]</code></td><td>Manage the self-healing monitor.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf notify &lt;ticket-id&gt; "&lt;text&gt;"</code></td><td>Post an alert to the ticket's Slack thread.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code class="hl">sssf viz [start|stop] [--port N] [--db PATH]</code></td><td>Run the global visualizer; the browser is the trace-reading surface.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</DocsLayout>
